  "aboutMe": {
    "profile": {
      "name": "Ferran",
      "surnames": "Buireu",
      "title": "Senior Software Engineer | Full-Stack & Data Architecture · TypeScript, React, Next.js, Go, AWS, Elasticsearch | Mentor",
      "description": "I lead the architecture of Gartner Peer Community: a Next.js frontend, Go services, and the AWS and Elasticsearch pipelines behind them. With over ten years in software engineering, my work today is full-stack in the literal sense, from data modelling and indexing decisions to the pages users interact with.\n\nI lead a team of three engineers and drive company-wide migrations from legacy platforms to modern, event-driven systems, working with stakeholders from Director to VP and GVP level. I have taken internal products from MVP to adoption by teams worldwide, and more recently I have been building AI agent skills and harnesses that automate recurring engineering work, such as vulnerability-driven dependency upgrades.\n\nAlongside engineering, I mentor. I have run more than 130 one-to-one sessions with over 60 engineers on MentorCruise and Codementor, both rated 5.0. Much of that work is career development: preparing for interviews, changing jobs, and making the step from mid-level to senior. I also conduct technical interviews at Gartner, which has led directly to new hires.\n\nI came to software from geophysics. My Master's thesis modelled subsurface structures from gravity measurements, and that training still shapes how I work: understand the system from the evidence available, then build on solid ground.\n\nOutside work, I play guitar, play football and train for marathons.",
