              {
                "description": "Technical lead for GPC (Gartner Peer Community): a high-traffic, data-intensive platform built around large-scale data ingestion, indexing, and search. I own architecture decisions end-to-end and lead a team of 3 engineers.\n\n- Own the platform's data architecture: defined and drove the migration from a MongoDB/S3 integration to an event-driven Elasticsearch pipeline, with blue-green indexing and data contracts agreed with Data Engineering.\n- Led several company-wide adoption and legacy-migration initiatives, planning phased rollouts and coordinating delivery with multiple Gartner teams.\n- Conceived and delivered an internal MVP that streamlined workflows for senior client-facing advisors; adoption spread organically, with teams worldwide requesting onboarding.\n- Partner with stakeholders from Director to VP and GVP level on scope, priorities, and technical direction.\n- Built AI agent skills and harnesses that automate recurring engineering work (e.g., vulnerability-driven dependency upgrades), removing team bottlenecks.\n- Set technical foundations and standards for new projects and MVPs; refactored legacy codebases for performance, SEO, and maintainability.\n- Technical interviewer: my interviews led directly to hires. Mentor engineers well beyond my own team."
